# Component State/Display Separation

Stateful components split into:

- **Display** — named export, pure props, no `useState`
- **State HOC** — `withX(WrappedComponent)`, owns state; default export is `withX(XDisplay)`

Both live in the same file. Stateless components need no split. Display controllers clone children to inject props rather than rendering fixed subtrees.

```jsx
export const FoldDisplay = ({ isOpen, toggle, children }) => { ... }

const withFold = (WrappedComponent) => ({ defaultOpen = false, ...props }) => {
  const [isOpen, setIsOpen] = useState(defaultOpen)
  const toggle = () => setIsOpen((prev) => !prev)
  return <WrappedComponent isOpen={isOpen} toggle={toggle} {...props} />
}

export default withFold(FoldDisplay)
```
